1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,816
Ever since you were little, did you feel a bit different from everyone else?

2
00:00:05,366 --> 00:00:08,677
A comment everyone else laughed off stayed with you for days.

3
00:00:08,878 --> 00:00:12,982
After being around a lot of people, you felt drained for no reason.

4
00:00:13,182 --> 00:00:16,782
And the path everyone said was good somehow never pulled at you.

5
00:00:17,332 --> 00:00:18,844
So you shrank back.

6
00:00:19,044 --> 00:00:20,196
Am I strange?

7
00:00:20,396 --> 00:00:21,728
Am I too sensitive?

8
00:00:22,278 --> 00:00:25,050
Today, I want to answer that feeling.

9
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:26,510
You're not strange.

10
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:30,922
Inside that difference, there's a power that's only yours.

11
00:00:31,472 --> 00:00:38,456
And I'll tell you the story of two people who changed the world with the very part of themselves others told them to fix.

12
00:00:39,606 --> 00:00:41,838
No two souls are the same.

13
00:00:42,388 --> 00:00:48,940
Each of us came here carrying the experiences we most want to have in this life, and the things we want to create on this Earth.

14
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:53,928
And we were born remembering, and holding on to, what we'd need for that.

15
00:00:54,478 --> 00:00:58,402
The traits that made you feel uncomfortable because you were different.

16
00:00:58,602 --> 00:01:00,870
The parts of you that you wanted to hide.

17
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:03,014
Those aren't broken pieces.

18
00:01:03,564 --> 00:01:12,816
They're your gifts, connected to what your soul came to focus on and experience more intensely in this life, and ultimately, to create here on Earth.

19
00:01:13,966 --> 00:01:19,042
Especially if you've often blamed yourself for being too sensitive, please hear this.

20
00:01:19,592 --> 00:01:32,840
After years of research, psychologist Elaine Aron found that about one in five people is born with a temperament that feels far more finely, and processes far more deeply, than others.

21
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:34,084
Not a flaw.

22
00:01:34,284 --> 00:01:35,688
A natural trait.

23
00:01:36,238 --> 00:01:39,694
People like this notice small changes others miss.

24
00:01:39,894 --> 00:01:46,338
They read what isn't said, they're moved more deeply by beauty, and they know how to stay beside someone who's hurting.

25
00:01:46,888 --> 00:01:49,084
That's why they tire easily, too.

26
00:01:49,284 --> 00:01:53,604
Not because they're weak, but because they're taking in that much.

27
00:01:54,754 --> 00:01:56,482
And there's this, too.

28
00:01:56,682 --> 00:02:02,622
Something others find hard, or don't even know how to do, that comes to you as easily as breathing.

29
00:02:03,172 --> 00:02:05,800
Putting a stranger at ease in minutes.

30
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,168
Seeing at a glance how to organize a mess.

31
00:02:09,368 --> 00:02:12,932
Knowing instantly whether colors and spaces work together.

32
00:02:13,132 --> 00:02:16,120
Sensing what someone feels without a word.

33
00:02:16,670 --> 00:02:19,946
These come so easily that you don't even realize they're gifts.

34
00:02:20,146 --> 00:02:23,782
Doesn't everyone do this, you think, and move on.

35
00:02:24,332 --> 00:02:25,052
No.

36
00:02:25,252 --> 00:02:26,728
Not everyone does.

37
00:02:26,928 --> 00:02:29,232
Your soul packed that on purpose.

38
00:02:30,382 --> 00:02:33,766
Susan Cain was a quiet, introverted child.

39
00:02:33,966 --> 00:02:37,962
People told her to be more outgoing, and she believed she had to be.

40
00:02:38,512 --> 00:02:43,372
So she acted like an extrovert, and worked as a Wall Street lawyer for seven years.

41
00:02:43,922 --> 00:02:50,618
Then she turned toward the very quietness she'd tried so hard to fix, and explored it deeply.

42
00:02:50,817 --> 00:02:59,565
The book she wrote, Quiet, brought comfort to introverts all over the world, and her talk has been watched by tens of millions of people.

43
00:03:00,116 --> 00:03:02,959
Animal scientist Temple Grandin is autistic.

44
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:08,811
As a child, she was late to speak, and being different made life very hard.

45
00:03:09,362 --> 00:03:12,674
But she thought in pictures, not words.

46
00:03:12,874 --> 00:03:16,186
So she could see what frightened animals before anyone else could.

47
00:03:16,386 --> 00:03:24,918
With that difference, she designed facilities where animals suffer less, and today, nearly half the cattle in America pass through them.

48
00:03:25,468 --> 00:03:29,356
The part of them that was different was exactly their power.

49
00:03:30,505 --> 00:03:35,545
And still we shrink back, because we measure ourselves with someone else's ruler.

50
00:03:36,095 --> 00:03:39,731
No one asks a rose to grow tall like a sunflower.

51
00:03:39,932 --> 00:03:43,244
No one asks a sunflower to smell like a rose.

52
00:03:43,444 --> 00:03:46,432
Each one simply blooms as itself.

53
00:03:46,982 --> 00:03:50,294
Compared to others, you'll always look a little strange.

54
00:03:50,494 --> 00:03:53,518
It was another flower's ruler to begin with.

55
00:03:54,068 --> 00:03:57,884
The only one who can measure you is your own soul.

56
00:03:59,034 --> 00:04:01,482
So how do you find your own gift?

57
00:04:01,682 --> 00:04:04,562
Ask yourself these four questions.

58
00:04:05,112 --> 00:04:05,796
One.

59
00:04:05,996 --> 00:04:09,668
When did I shrink back, thinking, am I strange?

60
00:04:09,868 --> 00:04:14,008
On the other side of that discomfort, a gift is often hiding.

61
00:04:14,558 --> 00:04:15,314
Two.

62
00:04:15,514 --> 00:04:20,266
What do others struggle with, that comes unusually easily to me?

63
00:04:20,816 --> 00:04:21,680
Three.

64
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:25,624
What do people keep asking me for, or asking me about?

65
00:04:26,174 --> 00:04:26,930
Four.

66
00:04:27,130 --> 00:04:30,226
As a child, what did I lose track of time doing?

67
00:04:30,776 --> 00:04:34,772
Where the answers overlap, that's where your gift lives.

68
00:04:35,922 --> 00:04:39,558
So starting today, try just three things.

69
00:04:40,108 --> 00:04:45,616
One, when you catch yourself thinking, am I strange, say this instead.

70
00:04:45,816 --> 00:04:48,120
This is a sign of my gift.

71
00:04:48,670 --> 00:04:53,710
Two, pick just one of the four questions today, and write down your answer.

72
00:04:54,260 --> 00:05:00,524
Three, once a day, instead of hiding what makes you different, let a little more of it show.

73
00:05:01,674 --> 00:05:04,086
So let's try it together, right now.

74
00:05:04,636 --> 00:05:07,192
Sit comfortably and close your eyes.

75
00:05:10,742 --> 00:05:12,398
Breathe in slowly…

76
00:05:16,598 --> 00:05:18,794
and breathe out, long.

77
00:05:24,344 --> 00:05:25,280
Once more.

78
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:27,136
Breathe in slowly…

79
00:05:31,336 --> 00:05:33,532
and breathe out, long.

80
00:05:39,082 --> 00:05:43,222
Think of one part of yourself that made you shrink back, because you were different.

81
00:05:49,772 --> 00:05:51,536
Don't push it away.

82
00:05:51,736 --> 00:05:53,716
Just look at it, gently.

83
00:05:59,266 --> 00:06:00,562
And say this to it.

84
00:06:00,762 --> 00:06:02,706
You were never strange.

85
00:06:08,256 --> 00:06:11,316
You were a gift my soul brought for this life.

86
00:06:17,866 --> 00:06:23,950
Now, feel that difference glowing as light, right in the center of your chest.

87
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:35,704
That light spreads through your whole body.

88
00:06:44,254 --> 00:06:47,494
There is only one light like this in the whole world.

89
00:06:53,044 --> 00:06:55,456
Now, take a deep breath in…

90
00:06:59,656 --> 00:07:03,292
and as you slowly breathe out, open your eyes.

91
00:07:07,442 --> 00:07:09,998
Being different doesn't mean being wrong.

92
00:07:10,198 --> 00:07:13,654
It means there's only one person like you in the whole world.

93
00:07:14,204 --> 00:07:18,632
The difference that made you uncomfortable, the parts you wanted to hide.

94
00:07:18,832 --> 00:07:22,576
Inside them is a power your soul has been holding onto.

95
00:07:23,126 --> 00:07:24,818
That is your greatest strength.

96
00:07:25,018 --> 00:07:29,878
And there are things only you can create on this Earth, because you are you.

97
00:07:30,428 --> 00:07:32,984
Now, stop shrinking.

98
00:07:33,184 --> 00:07:35,128
Bloom in your own light.

99
00:07:35,678 --> 00:07:40,538
In the comments, write one thing about yourself that's different, that you used to hide.

100
00:07:40,738 --> 00:07:42,574
It might just be your power.

101
00:07:43,124 --> 00:07:44,312
Play your own game.
